{
  "concept": "A decoder-only transformer predicts the next token at every position in parallel, using causally masked self-attention so each position sees only itself and earlier tokens.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Column heading: 'Word embeddings' over a dashed-outline container",
    "Column heading: 'Transformer with masked attention' over a grey rounded rectangle with dashed border",
    "Column heading: 'Linear + softmax'",
    "Column heading: 'Probability of target token'",
    "Left input token labels, top to bottom: <start>, It, takes, great, courage, to, let",
    "Seven horizontal arrows from the input token labels into the embedding container",
    "Seven word-embedding row vectors, each drawn as a row of ~6 empty white cells with black outlines, stacked vertically inside the dashed container",
    "Bracket/bus on the right of the embedding stack collecting all seven rows into one thick arrow entering the transformer block",
    "Masked self-attention panel: tall orange/salmon rounded rectangle containing a lower-triangular fan of straight connection lines from each source row to itself and all rows below it (causal pattern)",
    "Residual skip connection: black line routed over the top of the attention panel into a circled plus (⊕) node",
    "First circled plus (⊕) residual addition node after attention",
    "First teal vertical bar representing the post-attention layer-norm / feature vectors",
    "Position-wise feedforward group: seven small blue-grey rounded pill blocks stacked vertically, each fed by its own short arrow, wrapped by an outer routing rectangle",
    "Second residual skip connection routed over the feedforward group into a second circled plus (⊕)",
    "Second circled plus (⊕) residual addition node after the feedforward",
    "Second teal vertical bar representing the post-feedforward layer-norm output",
    "Annotation '(×K)' with a horizontal ellipsis '···' indicating the decoder block is repeated K times",
    "Seven teal rounded 'Linear + softmax' blocks, one per position, each fed by an arrow from the transformer output bus",
    "Seven output probability rows: blue-grey cells (three cells, dotted ellipsis, two more cells) representing a distribution over the whole vocabulary",
    "Vertical vocabulary axis labels under the first output row: a, aardvark, abacus, ···, zeta, zero",
    "Right-hand target-token labels, top to bottom: It, takes, great, courage, to, let, yourself",
    "Arrows connecting each Linear+softmax block to its probability row",
    "Tooltip/callout panel (appears on click) describing the role of the selected block"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "numLayers",
      "type": "slider",
      "teaches": "That the '(×K)' notation is shorthand for K identical stacked decoder blocks, each repeating masked attention + residual add + feedforward, and that depth is a design choice rather than part of the mechanism.",
      "label": "Decoder layers K",
      "range": [1, 6, 1],
      "default": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "maskMode",
      "type": "toggle",
      "teaches": "Why the attention pattern must be lower-triangular: with full bidirectional attention each position could read its own target token, so next-token prediction becomes trivial and the model learns nothing.",
      "label": "Attention pattern",
      "options": ["Causal mask", "Unmasked (all-to-all)"],
      "default": "Causal mask"
    },
    {
      "id": "inspectBlock",
      "type": "click",
      "teaches": "The distinct job of each stage — embedding lookup, masked mixing across positions, residual addition, and vocabulary projection — instead of treating the pipeline as one opaque box."
    },
    {
      "id": "tracePrediction",
      "type": "state",
      "teaches": "That the row for target 'yourself' is computed from the prefix '<start> … let' only, and that every other row is computed the same way simultaneously — one forward pass yields all next-token predictions.",
      "label": "Trace prediction of 'yourself'",
      "states": ["idle", "prefix", "attend", "residual", "softmax", "done"],
      "default": "idle"
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The pipeline at a glance",
      "narration": "Seven tokens enter as embedding vectors on the left and leave as seven probability distributions over the whole vocabulary on the right. Notice the output labels are the input sequence shifted by one: each position predicts the next token.",
      "state": { "numLayers": 1, "maskMode": "Causal mask", "tracePrediction": "idle" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Inside one decoder block",
      "narration": "Click the orange attention panel, the ⊕ nodes, and the teal bars: masked attention mixes information across positions, then each residual addition carries the original vector forward so the block only has to learn a correction.",
      "state": { "numLayers": 1, "maskMode": "Causal mask", "tracePrediction": "idle" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Why the triangle?",
      "narration": "Switch to unmasked attention and the connection fan fills in above the diagonal — now the vector at 'let' can see 'yourself', and predicting it is cheating. Switching back restores the lower-triangular causal mask.",
      "state": { "numLayers": 1, "maskMode": "Unmasked (all-to-all)", "tracePrediction": "idle" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Unrolling ×K",
      "narration": "Increase K and the single block expands into a stack of identical blocks. The shape of the computation never changes; only the number of times the sequence is re-mixed and refined.",
      "state": { "numLayers": 4, "maskMode": "Causal mask", "tracePrediction": "idle" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Tracing one prediction",
      "narration": "Step the trace: the prefix '<start> It takes great courage to let' lights up, attention lines flow only from those positions into the last row, residuals add, and the final Linear + softmax produces the distribution whose target is 'yourself'.",
      "state": { "numLayers": 4, "maskMode": "Causal mask", "tracePrediction": "attend" }
    },
    {
      "title": "All predictions at once",
      "narration": "Finish the trace and every row highlights: the same forward pass simultaneously predicts It, takes, great, courage, to, let and yourself — this parallel, shifted training is what makes decoder transformers efficient.",
      "state": { "numLayers": 4, "maskMode": "Causal mask", "tracePrediction": "done" }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "The lower-triangular attention pattern is the whole trick: it lets one parallel forward pass produce a next-token prediction at every position without any position ever peeking at its own answer.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Horizontal left-to-right pipeline on white background, four column headings in a serif/LaTeX-like font. Left: seven input token labels with arrows into a dashed-border container holding seven rows of ~6 empty outlined cells; a bracket funnels them into one thick arrow. Center: large light-grey rounded rectangle with dashed border, labelled 'Transformer with masked attention', containing (in order) a tall salmon/orange rounded panel filled with a lower-triangular fan of thin dark lines, a ⊕ node fed by a skip line routed over the panel, a slim teal vertical bar, a group of seven small blue-grey pill blocks each with its own feeder arrow and an outer routing rectangle, a second ⊕ with its own skip line, and a second teal bar. To its right, '(×K)' above a horizontal '···' and an arrow. Right: seven teal rounded 'Linear + softmax' blocks, each arrowing into a probability row of blue-grey cells (three cells, dotted gap, two cells); rotated vocabulary labels a / aardvark / abacus / ··· / zeta / zero beneath the first row; target labels It…yourself at the far right, visibly the input sequence shifted up by one. Highlighting should use a bright accent outline plus dimming of unselected blocks; the trace should pulse along arrows in orange. When K>1, draw repeated compact copies of the decoder block stacked horizontally (or vertically nested) with the '(×K)' badge replaced by layer indices 1…K."
}

